<attribute name="name" nodeId="e74f9ea1">Refine test types performed in each test level</attribute>
<attribute name="guid" nodeId="9f0178f8">_tuxKQB2cEeSDYtcxfT4ZFw</attribute>
<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="f3ebf7f3">Refine test types performed in each test level</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="f59d93b3"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="9c132f84">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="e9a75ef7"></attribute>
<attribute name="variabilityType" nodeId="3641ace2">na</attribute>
<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="36bdee50"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="df624b27">&lt;p&gt;
    Test types&amp;nbsp;represent the test&amp;nbsp;objectives fulfilled at each test level.&amp;nbsp;As target solution requirements
    are further defined, test types initially defined in the test strategy may need refinement. Collaborate with
    stakeholders to refine test objectives for test levels, as needed. For test types, there are various activities
    involved with every test type.&amp;nbsp;A detailed and clear plan defining sequence of those activities should be defined.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Additionally any specific techniques to be used for the different types of test at each level should be identified.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
