<attribute name="name" nodeId="8a3b512a">Define entry and exit criteria and acceptance thresholds</attribute>
<attribute name="guid" nodeId="ddc28c4c">_0ABF4B2cEeSDYtcxfT4ZFw</attribute>
<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="a483e296">Define entry and exit criteria and acceptance thresholds</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="ef3c4682"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="4bf4602b">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="370a2e02"></attribute>
<attribute name="variabilityType" nodeId="f5c149a1">na</attribute>
<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="beab86b5"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="7e1348e2">&lt;p&gt;
    For each test level and&amp;nbsp;type, define the entry and exit criteria, which determine start and stop points in test
    execution. Entry criteria requires that the proper environment is in place to support the upcoming test cycle. Exit
    criteria require that the solution under test has been satisfactorily completed before exiting the test level/type. To
    define entry and exit criteria, consideration must be given to the conditions&amp;nbsp;which must be satisfied before test
    execution can begin and when test execution can end. Entry and exit criteria should consider situations where time
    constraints necessitate overlapping test cycles.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Stakeholder consensus on entry and exit criteria prior to test execution is essential&amp;nbsp;for successful and timely
    completion of test effort. In conjunction with exit criteria, acceptance criteria for discovered defects is
    commonly&amp;nbsp;discussed with stakeholders. Acceptance criteria defines a tolerance level for defects that allows the
    test team to continue with the test effort should certain defects remain outstanding at the conclusion of a test type.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Perform the following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identify relevant test cycle
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Conduct risk assessment session with key stakeholders
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Conduct statistical analysis of defect impact on overall solution integrity
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Propose gate exit criteria
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Review configuration dependencies
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Review master data dependencies
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Conduct defect impact assessment
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Propose gate entry criteria
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Review test gate entry and exit criteria with all stakeholders
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Approve test gate entry and exit criteria
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Define test execution suspension and resumption criteria&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
