<attribute name="guid" nodeId="fc367b95">_CzassCWIEeSy_7093xOKuQ</attribute>
<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="ee01299e">Establish reporting and communication routines</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="1109c2d8"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="71606e4e">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="ea2d36ec"></attribute>
<attribute name="variabilityType" nodeId="1d3d8206">na</attribute>
<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="18dff84b"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="8cecddf8">&lt;p&gt;
    Discuss with stakeholders communication routines to be used for each test type. The goal is to come up with the number
    of meetings required to address identified risks and issues throughout the testing lifecycle and for easy coordination
    amongst different groups participating in the test effort. The frequency (twice a day, once a day, twice a week, etc.)
    of the meetings should also be discussed with stakeholders to allow for structured communication during testing.&amp;nbsp;
    The frequency (monthly, weekly, daily, etc.) of status reporting should also be discussed with stakeholders.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
