<attribute name="guid" nodeId="2517e299">_yJp4oJK1EeSEOeG-bGncjA</attribute>
<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="4d0e769c">Establish approach for training testers</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="2c2c0788"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="e1f47a59">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="5a5f317b"></attribute>
<attribute name="variabilityType" nodeId="74b5b415">na</attribute>
<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="9caf3a30"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="c851f49f">Discuss with stakeholders the approach to conduct training on the&amp;nbsp;target solution before test execution begins.
Training provides testers with a&amp;nbsp;holistic understanding of the target solution needed to perform a comprehensive test.
However, prioritizing certain&amp;nbsp;components of the target solution may be required based on limitations due to&amp;nbsp;test
scope, time and cost associated with training. Priority should be given to key aspects of the target solution that pose a
high risk of defects and thus require a large volume of testing to mitigate the risk.</attribute>
